'''Atul Auto Limited''' is an Indian [[three wheeler]] ([[auto rickshaw]], [[tuk-tuk]], [[e-rickshaw]]) manufacturing company based in [[Rajkot]].

== History ==
The company's origins lie in the 1970s, when Jagjivanbhai Chandra sought to modify motorcycles to make transport to meet the needs of rural areas of [[Saurashtra (region)|Saurashtra]], and adapted the engines from [[golf cart]]s scrapped by the Maharaja of Jamnagar, resulting in his first ''chhakada'' vehicles.<ref name="Forbes" /> The company incorporated in 1986,<ref>{{cite web|url=https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/atul-auto-ltd/infocompanyhistory/companyid-5864.cms|title=Atul Auto History - Atul Auto Information - The Economic Times|website=economictimes.indiatimes.com}}</ref> and production begin in 1992.<ref name="Forbes">{{Cite web|url=http://forbesindia.com/article/boardroom/atul-auto-riding-the-threewheeler-boom/38543/0|title=Forbes India - Atul Auto: Riding the Three-Wheeler Boom}}</ref>

Atul Auto has its manufacturing facilities at Rajkot and [[Ahmedabad]].<ref>{{cite news |title=Atul Auto forays into EV space, launches two electric three-wheelers |url=https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/industry/renewables/atul-auto-forays-into-ev-space-launches-two-electric-three-wheelers/articleshow/96911274.cms |access-date=28 February 2023 |work=The Economic Times |date=11 January 2023}}</ref>

